## Relay-Specific
# The port at which Tor will listen for incoming relay connections.
# Often 443, 9001, or another port that is not filtered by firewalls.
ORPort 9001

# Indicate whether this relay is allowed to be an "exit" node.
# Set to 0 to be a middle (non-exit) relay.
ExitRelay 0

# Provide a nickname for your relay (publicly visible).
Nickname SomeTorRelay

# Provide a valid admin contact email or URL for directory authorities
# and users to reach you if needed.
ContactInfo myemail@example.com

## Bandwidth Limits (Adjust to your capacity)
# Average bandwidth usage (bytes per second) that you want to allow.
# "100 KB" means ~800 kbps average.
RelayBandwidthRate 100 KB

# Max burst for short periods (bytes per second).
RelayBandwidthBurst 200 KB

## Other Common Options
# Disable local SOCKS proxy if you only want to run a relay.
SocksPort 0

## Data directory
DataDirectory /var/tor
